# Frontend Rules

## Design system (Yandex-Go-inspired — see docs/01-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md)
- Brand yellow `#FCE000` for hero surfaces, CTAs, and marketing panels. Near-black `#17181C` for text on yellow.
- Content sits on white rounded cards (`rounded-3xl`, 24px) floating over yellow or map surfaces.
- Service/collection tiles: white rounded squares in a responsive grid, icon top, label below — like a super-app home screen.
- Search is a pill (`rounded-full`) with a leading icon and a trailing action chip ("Where to?" pattern).
- Typography: heavy, tight headlines (`font-extrabold tracking-tight`); generous whitespace; sentence case.
- Motion: subtle scale on press (`active:scale-[0.98]`), 150–200ms transitions, no gratuitous animation.
- Use design tokens from `tailwind` theme config only. Never hardcode hex values in components.

## Accessibility (this is an accessibility product — hold the bar)
- All interactive elements keyboard-reachable, visible focus rings (`focus-visible:ring-2 ring-black`).
- Color contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for text. Yellow backgrounds always pair with near-black text.
- Trust states use icon + text, never color alone.
- MapLibre canvas gets an accessible fallback: place lists mirror map content.
- Forms: label every input, `aria-describedby` for errors, error text announced via `role="alert"`.
- Test with keyboard-only navigation before marking any page done.

## Components
- Reusable primitives in `src/components/ui/` (Button, Card, Chip, Badge, Sheet, Field).
- Map code isolated in `src/components/map/` — MapLibre never imported outside it.
- Route UI in `src/components/routing/` — controls grouped as "Must avoid" / "Prefer" / "Show on map".
- Every data component handles loading, empty, and error states explicitly. No spinner-only pages.

## i18n
- `src/lib/i18n/dictionaries/{uz,ru,en}.ts` — typed dictionary objects, `uz` is the source of truth.
- Dates/distances localized. Distances in meters/km.
